abstract: >-
  An engineering log and reproducible benchmark suite documenting the practical envelope of running modern open-weight large
  language models on a consumer-grade dual AMD Radeon AI PRO R9700 32 GB workstation (gfx1201, RDNA 4 / Navi 48) under ROCm 7.2
  and vLLM 0.19. The repository includes the v0.1 hardware-envelope preprint on Qwen 3.6 27B — covering the BF16-over-FP8
  quantisation-performance inversion of approximately 75 percent on gfx1201 and the absence of native FP8 kernels — METHODOLOGY.md,
  a reproducible Phase 1 envelope and Phase 2 scaling-sweep protocol, per-model software and hardware environment manifests, and
  aggregated benchmark summaries. Version 0.3.0 expands the model suite to twenty-one generation models (Qwen 3.5/3.6, the
  Bielik v3.0 family, PLLuM, Mistral/Mixtral and Kimi) and adds the Phase 2 v0.3 sweep harness with co-located TP=1 parallel
  execution and thermal and power instrumentation. Raw Phase 2 scaling data is under publication embargo; aggregated summaries
  and methodology are public. The intended audience is researchers preparing local AI infrastructure for privacy-sensitive
  workloads, hardware reviewers seeking reproducible methodology, and software maintainers working on RDNA 4 support in inference
  frameworks. Version 0.4.0 (2026-05-24) widens the scope from internal engineering log to public release pipeline: it adds the
  first public AWQ W4A16 vLLM-native quantization of the entire Llama-PLLuM-70B family (eight model cards and one reusable
  Polish clinical SmPC calibration dataset, on HuggingFace under the mozarcik namespace), a Phase 2 throughput sweep on six
  sanity-PASS variants of that family on the METHODOLOGY section 6 standard N grid, a documented Gate 2 human-verdict-override
  extension to the coherence-probe boundary in METHODOLOGY section 8, a new eval-rag sub-project (a five-model RAG benchmark of
  Polish versus multilingual LLMs on the SmPC corpus, with design and outreach drafts to potential co-authors), and a four-paper
  publication roadmap supporting a synthesis paper as the third pillar of the author's habilitation. Raw Phase 2 throughput
  numbers remain under publication embargo per METHODOLOGY section 11; engineering envelope, methodology, and external release
  artifacts are public.
